{
  "id": "web3-infra-self-healing",
  "name": "Web3 Infra Self-Healing Engine",
  "active": false,
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "287be078-55e2-4121-9ccb-4f2bfe668cb8",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -700,
        -180
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Web3 Infra Self-Healing Engine\n\nAn alert routes by service name into one of two diagnostic paths, gets a severity score from that diagnostic data, and branches through a human-in-the-loop approval gate before simulated self-healing runs. Diagnostics are deterministic simulations (derived from the incident ID); this never touches real blockchain or Kubernetes infrastructure.",
        "height": 160,
        "width": 700
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e4b33492-2dcf-404f-9f9c-5dcb98bf41c0",
      "name": "Alert Intake",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -700,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "web3-infra-self-healing",
        "responseMode": "responseNode",
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a804c768-e872-42b5-88ce-f7372516ac41",
      "name": "Normalize Incident Context",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        -460,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "manual",
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "n1",
              "name": "incident_id",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ ($json.body || $json).incident_id || ($json.body || $json).alert_id || ('ALERT-' + Date.now()) }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "n2",
              "name": "service_name",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ ($json.body || $json).service_name || \"unknown-service\" }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "n3",
              "name": "symptom",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ ($json.body || $json).symptom || ($json.body || $json).description || \"no symptom provided\" }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "includeOtherFields": false,
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "1189f378-8947-4262-bb66-30c383cc0c3e",
      "name": "Route by Failure Type",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.switch",
      "typeVersion": 3.2,
      "position": [
        -220,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "rules",
        "rules": {
          "values": [
            {
              "conditions": {
                "options": {
                  "caseSensitive": false,
                  "leftValue": "",
                  "typeValidation": "loose"
                },
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "id": "cond-protocol",
                    "leftValue": "={{ $json.service_name }}",
                    "rightValue": "node",
                    "operator": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "operation": "contains"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "combinator": "and"
              },
              "renameOutput": true,
              "outputKey": "protocol"
            },
            {
              "conditions": {
                "options": {
                  "caseSensitive": false,
                  "leftValue": "",
                  "typeValidation": "loose"
                },
                "conditions": [
                  {
                    "id": "cond-infra",
                    "leftValue": "={{ $json.service_name }}",
                    "rightValue": "api",
                    "operator": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "operation": "contains"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "combinator": "and"
              },
              "renameOutput": true,
              "outputKey": "infra"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {
          "fallbackOutput": "extra",
          "renameFallbackOutput": "infra"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "6cd9b70e-de9e-447f-bc4a-ea3da1918447",
      "name": "Protocol Path Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        40,
        20
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "**Protocol path.** Taken when the service name looks like a blockchain node. Simulates checking RPC sync lag and peer count, deterministic per incident ID, so the same incident always produces the same (reproducible) diagnostic result.",
        "height": 140,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "90bab467-680c-470a-bf01-1e4650f94699",
      "name": "Check RPC Sync",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        40,
        180
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "\n// Simulated diagnostic (this repo never touches real validator/RPC\n// infrastructure) but the logic genuinely runs: derive a deterministic\n// \"block lag\" from the incident id so different incidents produce\n// different, reproducible results instead of a static stub.\nconst item = $input.item.json;\nlet hash = 0;\nfor (const ch of item.incident_id) hash = (hash * 31 + ch.charCodeAt(0)) >>> 0;\nconst blockLag = hash % 40;\nconst rpcHealthy = blockLag < 12;\nreturn [{ json: { ...item, block_lag: blockLag, rpc_healthy: rpcHealthy } }];\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "05e871c3-3cb8-45e7-8097-096bef92c671",
      "name": "Scan Peer/Log Signal",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        280,
        180
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "\nconst item = $input.item.json;\nlet hash = 0;\nfor (const ch of item.incident_id) hash = (hash * 17 + ch.charCodeAt(0)) >>> 0;\nconst peerCount = 8 + (hash % 20);\nconst peersHealthy = peerCount >= 12;\nreturn [{ json: { ...item, peer_count: peerCount, peers_healthy: peersHealthy, diagnostic_path: 'protocol' } }];\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "0e547a65-da66-4058-a5da-f0f9b793da74",
      "name": "Infra Path Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        40,
        600
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "**Infra path.** Taken when the service name looks like a regular API/backend service. Simulates a Kubernetes pod-restart count and a log error rate, with the same determinism guarantee as the protocol path.",
        "height": 140,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "70730dbb-c095-4000-b8f3-2e08afecbb48",
      "name": "Worker: K8s Context",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        40,
        420
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "\n// Simulated K8s describe summary -- deterministic per incident, not a stub.\nconst item = $input.item.json;\nlet hash = 0;\nfor (const ch of item.incident_id) hash = (hash * 13 + ch.charCodeAt(0)) >>> 0;\nconst restartCount = hash % 6;\nconst podHealthy = restartCount < 3;\nreturn [{ json: { ...item, pod_restart_count: restartCount, pod_healthy: podHealthy } }];\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "330c16ed-b621-4a00-9844-4a6c976d64ba",
      "name": "Worker: Log Analysis",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        280,
        420
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "\nconst item = $input.item.json;\nlet hash = 0;\nfor (const ch of item.incident_id) hash = (hash * 23 + ch.charCodeAt(0)) >>> 0;\nconst errorRatePercent = hash % 25;\nconst logsHealthy = errorRatePercent < 8;\nreturn [{ json: { ...item, error_rate_percent: errorRatePercent, logs_healthy: logsHealthy, diagnostic_path: 'infra' } }];\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2d898ae1-a28d-4fe1-a0ac-1d9a9f92a900",
      "name": "Compute Severity Score",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        540,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "\nconst item = $input.item.json;\nconst healthyFlags = [item.rpc_healthy, item.peers_healthy, item.pod_healthy, item.logs_healthy].filter((v) => v !== undefined);\nconst unhealthyCount = healthyFlags.filter((v) => v === false).length;\nconst severity = unhealthyCount === 0 ? 'low' : unhealthyCount === 1 ? 'medium' : 'high';\nconst escalation_required = severity === 'high';\nreturn [{ json: { ...item, severity, escalation_required } }];\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "0e685508-b9d1-4b69-9711-25a08c0abbcc",
      "name": "Approval Gate Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        780,
        -180
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "**Human-in-the-loop.** High-severity incidents (2+ unhealthy diagnostics) wait for a mocked senior-TSE approval; everything else auto-approves. The approval itself is mocked (no real paging/Slack integration wired up), but the branching logic is real.",
        "height": 160,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "17e9227d-d1fa-4ee7-8ecd-1703ce22e6f1",
      "name": "Senior TSE Approval Gate",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        780,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict"
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "cond-escalation",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.escalation_required }}",
              "rightValue": true,
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "915ef6da-4797-4df2-b28f-d45c15e54d09",
